# Theme Management — Colors Are Admin-Managed, Not Static

Full reference: `starter-kit/22-theme-management.md`. Every color the site renders comes from the `theme-settings` global (admin, per mode: dark/light) via CSS custom properties — not a static Tailwind hex.

## Rules

- **Never hardcode a color** — no raw hex (`bg-[#1A1A1A]`, `style={{ color: '#fff' }}`), no arbitrary Tailwind color value. Use the existing token classes: `bg-brand-500`, `text-neutral-400`, `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `text-semantic-error`, `border-accent-blue`, etc.
- **Need a color that doesn't exist yet?** Add it to `THEME_TOKEN_DEFS` in `src/lib/theme/tokens.ts` (+ both mode defaults) and the matching `var(--color-...)` in `tailwind.config.js` — never invent a one-off hex instead.
- **`tailwind.config.js` `colors` values must all be `var(--color-...)`** — never a static hex added back in.
- Scope is color only — radius/shadow/spacing/typography stay static; don't extend this pattern to those without a deliberate design decision.

## Review gate

- [ ] No raw hex or inline color style introduced
- [ ] Any new color went through `THEME_TOKEN_DEFS` first
- [ ] `tailwind.config.js` colors stay 100% `var(--color-...)` references

